:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bed4ba0-143c-55e4-8b94-cc1adbfedf1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bed4ba0-143c-55e4-8b94-cc1adbfedf1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298089} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd67c8a-ac92-5c47-a537-dcfda01bbe7f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298843} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a80034ba-1744-5a46-b6b5-2ed8aaaa8697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a80034ba-1744-5a46-b6b5-2ed8aaaa8697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298286} :answer-field/id #uuid "abd4db80-2ac5-562f-8418-30c4cf225d25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbad9be4-81c3-5d76-a5dd-452794f75baa" :question/math-academy-id "q-320351" :question/problem "Let\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$D=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nThen, the dimensions of $CD$ are <span style=\"display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .35em; white-space: nowrap;\">{{field-1}} $\\times$ {{field-2}}</span>." :question/worked-solution "We notice that $C$ is a $4\\times 1$ matrix and $D$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $C$ and $1$ row in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $C$ equals the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $CD$ has dimensions $4\\times 3:$\n\n$$\n{C}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{D}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3}={CD}_{4\\times 3}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2ac3c5c-f6cd-5fd5-b2a0-6cb8e37b78ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2ac3c5c-f6cd-5fd5-b2a0-6cb8e37b78ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298329} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ce7fe03-ed70-594f-8d42-ac888b8e9609" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298955} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2266199c-ddd0-5fc1-8ad7-a0c747f7e74d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2266199c-ddd0-5fc1-8ad7-a0c747f7e74d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297699} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfce6c8e-4282-53ef-a878-8e11c69a3c7c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cef63f89-6766-5942-a14a-b8ab45d7b4ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-320371" :question/problem "Let\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$E=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nThen, the dimensions of $FE$ are <span style=\"display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .35em; white-space: nowrap;\">{{field-1}} $\\times$ {{field-2}}</span>." :question/worked-solution "We notice that $E$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix and $F$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $F$ and $4$ rows in $E.$ Since the number of columns in $F$ equals the number of rows in $E,$ the matrices $F$ and $E$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $FE$ has dimensions $2\\times 2:$\n\n$$\n{F}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{E}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={FE}_{2\\times 2}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b531995-3719-5c05-9a3c-e478fed52731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b531995-3719-5c05-9a3c-e478fed52731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297861} :answer-field/id #uuid "354c79d4-07d9-5b3b-a3ee-14567f83010b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0db2944-4924-5aea-9ee1-3438dd657d1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0db2944-4924-5aea-9ee1-3438dd657d1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298515} :answer-field/id #uuid "77c35a34-4f54-59b4-9538-e689eff39b82" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "283919b2-9c02-5df9-b56d-dbcf89785d7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-320389" :question/problem "Let\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$E=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nThen, the dimensions of $EF$ are <span style=\"display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .35em; white-space: nowrap;\">{{field-1}} $\\times$ {{field-2}}</span>." :question/worked-solution "We notice that $E$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix and $F$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. \n\nThere are $2$ columns in $E$ and $2$ rows in $F.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $F,$ the matrices $E$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $EF$ has dimensions $3\\times 1:$ \n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 1}={EF}_{3\\times 1}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329644 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e232d15-a82e-5bae-ad4e-7151f902a03c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450630} {:answer/id #uuid "016d62d0-b45f-56de-ac7a-54959e9d1014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e232d15-a82e-5bae-ad4e-7151f902a03c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450630} :answer-field/id #uuid "69857d61-3c1e-5f25-b16c-ae8c4b26a97b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86b72976-dc85-5a33-9be2-c83670ec7e09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450632} {:answer/id #uuid "283d41dd-3b3f-5bd7-9eed-4933fde66ce2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "283d41dd-3b3f-5bd7-9eed-4933fde66ce2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450633} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3cf63d8-da92-5363-889b-bd55efe17b6d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451270} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caca7f8a-73a6-5713-9718-8a9f3a6ffce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450634} {:answer/id #uuid "38fd2b25-e69d-5619-b54c-39f7cb6d92d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caca7f8a-73a6-5713-9718-8a9f3a6ffce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450634} :answer-field/id #uuid "67959733-2425-566d-8885-d0d38ff4a97c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e92499c-048f-53fc-971b-21b3cc496d2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42375" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$J=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$K=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$L=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $J,K,$ and $L?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $JK$ is well defined\n- **II.** The product $KL$ is well defined\n- **III.** The product $JL$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $J$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, $K$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $L$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $J$ and $3$ rows in $K.$ Since the number of columns in $J$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $K,$ the matrices $J$ and $K$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{J}_{3\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{K}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $K$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $K$ equals the number of rows in $L$, the matrices $K$ and $L$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{K}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{L}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $J$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $J$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $L$, the matrices $J$ and $L$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{J}_{3\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{L}_{2\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement II is true, while statements I and III are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2471c953-6866-5f30-b8fb-642d99c1ace1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450636} {:answer/id #uuid "1416b89a-9a9c-5884-826f-ae30875cf015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1416b89a-9a9c-5884-826f-ae30875cf015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450637} :answer-field/id #uuid "a705e15a-d1e7-5bf3-b4aa-b691e120e372" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451272} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8447ddfe-be0d-5b71-bcfb-c8ec6a527840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450638} {:answer/id #uuid "f32de81a-a67d-5c05-a23b-408b4c24c94f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8447ddfe-be0d-5b71-bcfb-c8ec6a527840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450638} :answer-field/id #uuid "89a2e509-982e-5827-9916-480316d7a0d4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451273} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbe86f27-2181-598c-a9d5-19eb645c28d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450640} {:answer/id #uuid "8e864ad0-6589-5362-b1e0-e291187efcad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e864ad0-6589-5362-b1e0-e291187efcad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450641} :answer-field/id #uuid "618ce025-20da-5809-a4f2-b304969686e3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca108716-0018-5080-8610-49601a0656af" :question/math-academy-id "q-42376" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$D=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$E=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $D,E,$ and $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $ED$ is well defined\n- **II.** The product $FD$ is well defined\n- **III.** The product $EF$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, $E$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $F$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $E$ and $2$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $E$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{D}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $F$ and $2$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $F$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $F$ and $D$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{F}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{D}_{2\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $E$ and $2$ rows in $F.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $F,$ the matrices $E$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca8eb228-c1aa-526c-bf90-27f66a9356c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450642} {:answer/id #uuid "bd87b62f-9da3-5f73-ab7a-d82a98e30bc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca8eb228-c1aa-526c-bf90-27f66a9356c3" :answer/type {:db/id #