.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e41c04ee-99fe-56c1-8773-ea0949cc66d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-42377" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$L=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$N=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $L,M,$ and $N?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $ML$ is well defined\n- **II.** The product $MN$ is well defined\n- **III.** The product $LN$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $L$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $M$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $N$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $M$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $M$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $L,$ the matrices $M$ and $L$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{M}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{L}_{2\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $M$ and $3$ rows in $N.$ Since the number of columns in $M$ equals the number of rows in $N,$ the matrices $M$ and $N$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{M}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{N}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $L$ and $3$ rows in $N.$ Since the number of columns in $L$ equals the number of rows in $N,$ the matrices $L$ and $N$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{L}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{N}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are true, while statement I is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329647 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b747550b-0a4a-5f3d-86b4-30ddaca87768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450648} {:answer/id #uuid "f90dfbaa-1eb7-5028-8821-63442d778562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f90dfbaa-1eb7-5028-8821-63442d778562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450649} :answer-field/id #uuid "623efc55-bdf4-53da-9936-ec2df1772b9d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7ca6a7b-d2c1-579c-8b4e-c3fc51e76679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450650} {:answer/id #uuid "460bc98c-aa4d-5008-abd2-b4b13e84f625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7ca6a7b-d2c1-579c-8b4e-c3fc51e76679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450650} :answer-field/id #uuid "5059dfed-f97b-5c68-860f-943b60870dcb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451279} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20fd12d0-0b82-5d63-b678-fdb08097e4e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450652} {:answer/id #uuid "dd3ba80b-43c0-5469-926f-886110b94004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20fd12d0-0b82-5d63-b678-fdb08097e4e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450652} :answer-field/id #uuid "d414d56d-e135-5893-a7d7-26e4a83fd3f2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "628bddc5-7db2-5c2d-bca2-c9a2f11c4f87" :question/math-academy-id "q-42381" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$O=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $OP$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $OR$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $PR$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $P$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $O$ and $2$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $O$ and $1$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $O$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $P$ and $1$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statements II and III are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f38167e2-3c1d-5c00-9691-ba8e6ac6fdce" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices Given the Dimensions of the Factors" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447a88e0-6091-5ac0-9834-0b06c2b6da42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336671} {:answer/id #uuid "5761b146-8cbf-5d87-97ae-a54747bdf58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336835} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0d3dd2-c61b-5322-93f0-d47718dacdc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337156} {:answer/id #uuid "906ba5cf-0c86-5c6a-a079-c82f2917e945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337341} {:answer/id #uuid "ca878198-1b18-5ab0-904e-b20db81eaa43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d0d3dd2-c61b-5322-93f0-d47718dacdc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337156} :answer-field/id #uuid "f500dc70-4e92-501f-8efc-78d25f2de91e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338706}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa2d5d03-0bdc-5285-8af4-0669d6c81891" :question/math-academy-id "q-70702" :question/problem "Suppose $R$ is a $4\\times 5$ matrix and $S$ is a  $2\\times 4$ matrix. What are the dimensions of $SR?$" :question/worked-solution "There are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication, and $SR$ is a $2\\times 5$ matrix:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 5}={SR}_{2\\times 5}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345301 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7f860f4-816a-5393-ae9d-2ecb0c1f468c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343716} {:answer/id #uuid "af921b50-e88f-5ebd-b3e2-dba22eb65847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343782} {:answer/id #uuid "bd8558fc-a4cc-539d-b781-9288c5ab8bdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343906} {:answer/id #uuid "c2bd3920-bd82-5ac0-9594-335890c16575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343952} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6ccab9-827b-5ef9-8d9f-1b7428deeac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec6ccab9-827b-5ef9-8d9f-1b7428deeac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344314} :answer-field/id #uuid "dae74c21-b257-59e4-b24c-655b2133233b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e32d224-c2ec-5642-95ee-f28fd98abe68" :question/math-academy-id "q-77475" :question/problem "Let\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhat are the dimensions of $YU?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that $Y$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix and $U$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $Y$ and $3$ rows in $U.$ Since the number of columns in $Y$ equals the number of rows in $U,$ the matrices $Y$ and $U$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $YU$ has dimensions $1\\times 1:$\n\n$$\n{Y}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{U}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 1}={YU}_{1\\times 1}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60592584-71a9-5dab-888c-405420e985f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403887} {:answer/id #uuid "803bf64e-e7ce-576c-8d72-84fb237b0900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403888} {:answer/id #uuid "1d361957-5943-53dc-96fc-7cd9606514fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403889} {:answer/id #uuid "458d1885-5503-53b8-ada5-bebd8ce461d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403890} {:answer/id #uuid "a526ff5b-3dc1-5b6f-891e-1cefb24bf872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "458d1885-5503-53b8-ada5-bebd8ce461d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403890} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bc81805-e6d6-540d-8f35-85fe2c75a075" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9bc6ac30-b2f0-52c3-a082-54b213e2ff6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-77476" :question/problem "Let\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$E=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\sqrt{3} & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhat are the dimensions of $ER?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that $E$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix and $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $E$ and $1$ row in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $E$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $ER$ has dimensions $3\\times 3:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3}={ER}_{3\\times 3}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a87fd5f-5da7-5d6d-8f82-03766fd4d889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521660} {:answer/id #uuid "266eca8d-bb57-5595-a7bd-99a7201356c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\times 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521662} {:answer/id #uuid "2eb35eaa-99e6-5220-9da6-e00da58e1695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521663} {:answer/id #uuid "7027a073-5ded-54d6-b9a0-2164504284eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521667} {:answer/id #uuid "ca13d901-1026-5387-b643-a90c7fd8b3c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "266eca8d-bb57-5595-a7bd-99a7201356c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\times 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521662} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbda40b9-522d-5acc-90dd-c56a10197af7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "618f58a8-e1e1-5e32-9c15-6b3c70021057" :question/problem "Let\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $4\\times 4:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 4}={BA}_{4\\times 4}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521672 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21e735e3-56fa-56a4-9de2-41c04f1cce64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\times 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521661} {:answer/id #uuid "5e942903-ca47-5490-bad7-5c09c559bf53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521665} {:answer/id #uuid "8f222be0-20c4-5fb7-8cbe-34004339c4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521668} {:answer/id #uuid "96ad16a3-53da-50b3-a8c1-99db611ab848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521669} {:answer/id #uuid "ca91aed1-c788-55f1-aa33-6f49a17a175e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21e735e3-56fa-56a4-9de2-41c04f1cce64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\times 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521661} :answer-field/id #uuid "5067c690-b5a5-54d3-a575-8f7580af4b10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f6737145-cc51-5a3f-8717-a40f740175a3" :question/problem "Let\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that $A$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $2$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $4\\times 4:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}={BA}_{4\\times 4}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076c6b2a-e1d0-5505-b700-bcf004ce4d75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562854} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7f3c0d-6cd0-5f80-8b00-c608989978ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "076c6b2a-e1d0-5505-b700-bcf004ce4d75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562854} :answer-field/id #uuid "1073773b-df59-5220-8043-a441e8a3b974" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fc9c401-1e65-5873-89b4-5ede83dca30d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562888} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7fd980-eed2-51e5-9c91-bb2c4b24efb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd7fd980-eed2-51e5-9c91-bb2c4b24efb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562921} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1b98f72-cdd0-540c-895f-00b0413680c5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4607e018-576d-516c-bd98-9f6231ff371d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562867} {:answer/id #uuid "5e879290-41ce-5caa-9a80-54fb5adc6df8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e879290-41ce-5caa-9a80-54fb5adc6df8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562875} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbcce078-a3f1-5646-afef-3c0d9a54a619" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "514aa297-d018-5213-8e1d-3b49622a8fe3" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$O=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & -5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $OP$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $PR$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $PO$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $1\\times 4$ row vector, $P$ is a $5\\times 1$ column vector, and $R$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $O$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{1\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{5\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there is $1$ column in $P$ and $5$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{5\\times 1}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{5\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there is $1$ column in $P$ and $1$ row in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $P$ and $O$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{5\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{O}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562872 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f4356be-29f1-5e2b-830b-308a53df5c34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562882} {:answer/id #uuid "85c9a81f-67cf-5cc7-90ed-a7b1dbdd973d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f4356be-29f1-5e2b-830b-308a53df5c34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562882} :answer-field/id #uuid "63b06bda-1c4c-596d-b2b7-2455e8bb3e84" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c2fb6f9-03f7-5731-ba5a-e3e4edd662b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562868} {:answer/id #uuid "4d370fc6-4fed-5c27-900c-ba8012cedd47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d370fc6-4fed-5c27-900c-ba8012cedd47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562869} :answer-field/id #uuid "b42c3153-374b-54ee-86c7-d7414ae8c1d5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562899} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "934a6aee-e168-56ff-aaa0-3c4a7d248df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562890} {:answer/id #uuid "db1d43c6-c9b4-5900-96b1-0aa4ef8e6ae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "934a6aee-e168-56ff-aaa0-3c4a7d248df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562890} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb318e8d-7c03-55c8-bc35-aa74f911f214" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "55f9a3f4-1446-576a-9dd6-8f5cec99c326" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$O=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $OR$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $PO$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $OP$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector, $P$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector, and $R$ is a $5\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere is $1$ column in $O$ and $5$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $O$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times 1}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{5\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $P$ and $3$ rows in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $P$ and $O$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{O}_{3\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there is $1$ column in $O$ and $1$ row in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562881 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34dafa4d-3944-582e-bbf7-64a2dcc62647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562862} {:answer/id #uuid "d55b794e-24e2-5354-bfec-ef76085b2a8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d55b794e-24e2-5354-bfec-ef76085b2a8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562909} :answer-field/id #uuid "3045f8ab-525f-5485-b581-68eae6f98ef3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34e4c5ce-7e9c-5530-8b6b-ec090d2ebab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562863} {:answer/id #uuid "a87f780f-4b8f-5015-b434-03be4bcc01d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34e4c5ce-7e9c-5530-8b6b-ec090d2ebab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562863} :answer-field/id #uuid "45d02062-6090-52e6-a662-c6361863dc12" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562865} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a4cd583-5b45-56dc-a6e1-195b989eb2a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562858} {:answer/id #uuid "63547524-da22-5745-afb6-a330347919c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a4cd583-5b45-56dc-a6e1-195b989eb2a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562858} :answer-field/id #uuid "8307eb05-c0ad-51ff-8381-69c2aa369a62" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "795f6284-9977-53c9-b26a-515ee6438422" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$O=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -6 & -9 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -9 & 4 & 2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 4 & -4 & -8 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -3 & -7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $RO$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $PR$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $RP$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $4\\times 5$ matrix, $P$ is a $1\\times 4$ row vector, and $R$ is a $2\\times 1$ column vector.\n\nThere is $1$ column in $R$ and $4$ rows in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $R$ and $O$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2\\times 1}{\\times }_{\\ne }{O}_{4\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $P$ and $2$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{2\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there is $1$ column in $R$ and $1$ row in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562887 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02a6580c-0d89-558b-b971-11e565184416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562853} {:answer/id #uuid "32a9097c-5bc2-5cd1-9baa-bd8b990c97fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32a9097c-5bc2-5cd1-9baa-bd8b990c97fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562861} :answer-field/id #uuid "131a6720-5179-5e6b-8f36-e30376510b3e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58588f5a-9b68-55e3-be19-a5e5b6a4cf7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562873} {:answer/id #uuid "9feee51e-8401-51e5-96ac-227b7313667d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9feee51e-8401-51e5-96ac-227b7313667d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562893} :answer-field/id #uuid "45d82d62-d901-5b62-a460-0db146091d33" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562866} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "783b131e-8f12-50a4-83d7-9f8aaca679d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562880} {:answer/id #uuid "b095e79b-a819-586b-ab09-7239d584f9f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b095e79b-a819-586b-ab09-7239d584f9f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562897} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e7a67a5-a17a-53dc-81ea-712acf4793d9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8c1748bb-90d6-5563-8ef1-b046b936907d" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$O=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -9 & -4 & -6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 8 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $OR$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $OP$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $RO$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector, $P$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix, and $R$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector.\n\nThere are $5$ columns in $O$ and $3$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $O$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{1\\times 5}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{3\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $5$ columns in $O$ and $4$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{1\\times 5}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{4\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there is $1$ column in $R$ and $1$ row in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $R$ and $O$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{O}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 5}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6a813dd-19f7-54e1-a2c7-bd667d5aed30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562903} {:answer/id #uuid "e19500d1-8755-5dc6-ac50-746ede9424ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e19500d1-8755-5dc6-ac50-746ede9424ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562915} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d51da39-0b01-536b-bfb2-eec56fd78de6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8d70d25-2c3a-51bc-ba52-e7054852cfb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562911} {:answer/id #uuid "f069bd38-0367-5fd7-9bc6-9d965655353a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f069bd38-0367-5fd7-9bc6-9d965655353a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562917} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c7e2a8e-c431-5d07-a1c8-050d821fbc8f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562891} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ef90c50-c0ed-5d96-9665-4922437d58f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562859} {:answer/id #uuid "bd996ffd-f797-5509-9bbe-b47b6aeefa46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ef90c50-c0ed-5d96-9665-4922437d58f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562859} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3c54a46-9187-506d-a306-7298aa00b5a1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "93240880-0a92-5ff3-9e93-67e683dcedec" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$O=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -5 & -8 & -8 \\\\ -5 & -2 & 8 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $RP$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $PR$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $OP$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, $P$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector, and $R$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector.\n\nThere is $1$ column in $R$ and $1$ row in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $P$ and $3$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{3\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $O$ and $1$ row in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{2\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{1\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statements II and III are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562892 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3edafb7e-5a8e-568e-93a2-d9776a6084b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562864} {:answer/id #uuid "f014b7fd-ab32-5bb4-a516-8d9a267ee4fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f014b7fd-ab32-5bb4-a516-8d9a267ee4fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562916} :answer-field/id #uuid "b19a20c5-afb7-5dc2-9fc1-9c594316a164" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562898} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5bd226a-d5ac-511a-968f-be677f0cb766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186